schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-UISETUP
wu: E-UISETUP.W6
tests:
  unit:
    count: 15
    covers: "Rust store.rs (+1): note_connection increments connection_count and broadcasts ConnectionSeen { authority }, and the count is independent of flow inserts/evictions. Rust api/view.rs (+1 case in sse_event_shapes): ConnectionSeen maps to event name 'connection' with { authority }. TS setup.test.ts (+11): the status-derivation functions return the right row of the plan's tables for every (probe, decrypted, traffic, running/error) combination — trustStatus (probe-trusted green; decrypted-proves-trust green even when probe can't; traffic-not-decrypting = warn pointing at the sending device; un-probeable = can't-check not 'not set up'; probed-untrusted-nothing-seen = calm muted; installing/failed transients), proxyStatus (probe-ours or ANY connection = green; nothing-yet vs can't-check distinct), verifyStatus (green only on a decrypted flow, traffic alone is not decrypt), and proveItSnippet carries the real address never a hardcoded port. TS Onboarding.test.tsx status/P1/P3 (+1 net; several rewritten): the honest status line renders per derivation (trusted->ok, untrusted+traffic->warn device-hint, connection->proxy green, un-probeable->can't-check), a failed action shows warn in its status line not a false done, the Verify prove-it renders the concrete curl with the real address as copyable text, and P3 puts the manual steps behind a 'Set it up manually' disclosure on an auto OS (inline on a non-auto OS)."
  integration:
    count: 3
    covers: "Core contract (tests/e2e_capture.rs +1): against a real ephemeral core, a client that does NOT trust the CA fails its intercepted TLS handshake and records NO flow, yet bumps GET /stats connections AND emits a 'connection' SSE event carrying the target authority; the trusted-https and plain-http paths (existing) still yield the expected flows. tests/api.rs (+1): GET /stats reports the note_connection tally. App seam (App.test.tsx +1): a 'connection' event turns the proxy step green ('Receiving traffic', data-tone ok) while trust shows the not-decrypting device hint, and neither a probe nor a bare connection ever reveals the flow list — reveal stays decrypted-flow-only."
  e2e:
    count: 4
    covers: "ui/e2e/specs/onboarding.spec.ts: the UC-5 spine stays green with the new render — fresh launch shows onboarding (step-trust-ca/step-verify), a real proxied+decrypted HTTPS request flips Verify green and reveals the list, then the list filters and appends live."
  waived: "The two local OS probes (ca_trusted via 'security'/'certutil'; proxy_status reused from W5 via 'networksetup'/registry) read the real machine trust store / system proxy and are not hermetically runnable — same class as W2/W3's auto-set commands, epic waiver inherited. Their behaviour is a thin shell-out returning trusted/untrusted/unknown; the STATUS DERIVATION they feed is fully unit-tested in TS, and the connection signal they complement IS hermetic (a real CONNECT at an ephemeral core) and proven at integration with no waiver. The connection-goes-green-before-decrypt path is asserted at integration, not re-driven in the WebDriver e2e (the harness only drives a trusted proxied request)."
